_meanings:
.²1 The soul, the individual soul, the breath, the principle of life and
 sensation; {#kimAtmanA yo na jitendriyo Bavet#} <ls>H. 1</ls>; {#AtmAnaM raTinaM#}
 {#vidDi SarIraM raTameva tu#} <ls>Kaṭh. 3. 3</ls>. (In {#AtmA nadI saMyamapuRyatIrTA#}
 <ls>H. 4. 87</ls> {#Atman#} is compared to a river).
.²2 Self, oneself; in this sense mostly used reflexively for all three
 persons and in the singular number, masculine gender, whatever be the gender
 or number of the noun to which it refers; {#anayA cintayAtmApi me na pratiBAti#}
 <ls>Ratn. 1</ls>; {#ASramadarSanena AtmAnaM punImahe#} <ls>Ś. 1</ls>; {#guptaM dadfSurAtmAnaM#}
 {#sarvAH svapnezu vAmanEH#} <ls>R. 10. 60</ls>, <ls n="R.">4. 35</ls>, <ls n="R.">14. 57</ls>; <ls>Ku. 6. 20</ls>; {#devI#}
 {#… prAptaprasavamAtmAnaM gaNgAdevyAM vimuYcati#} <ls>U. 7. 2</ls>; {#gopAyanti#}
 {#kulastriya AtmAnamAtmanA#} <ls>Mb.</ls>; <ls>K. 107</ls>; sometimes used in <ab>pl.</ab> also; {#AtmanaH#}
 {#stuvanti#} <ls>Śi. 17. 19</ls>; <ls>Māl. 8</ls>.
.²3 Supreme deity and soul of the universe, Supreme Soul, Brahman; {#tasmAdvA#}
 {#etasmAdAtmana AkASaH saMBUtaH#} <ls>T. Up. 2. 1. 1</ls>; <ls>Ms. 1. 15</ls>, <ls n="Ms.">12. 24</ls>.
.²4 Essence, nature; {#kAvyasyAtmA DvaniH#} <ls>S. D.</ls>, see {#Atmaka#} below.
.²5 Character, peculiarity; {#AtmA yakzmasya naSyati#} <ls>Rv. 10. 97. 11</ls>.
.²6 The natural temperament or disposition; <ls>Bhāg. 11. 22. 20</ls>.
.²7 The person or whole body (considered as one and opposed to the separate
 members of it); {#sTitaH sarvonnatenorvI krAntvA merurivAtmanA#} <ls>R. 1. 14</ls>;
 {#yosyAtmanaH kArAyitA#} <ls>Ms. 12. 12</ls>; <ls>Ki. 9. 66</ls>.
.²8 Mind, intellect; {#mandAtman, nazwAtman, mahAtman#} <ab>&c.</ab> {#aTa rAmaH#}
 {#prasannAtmA SrutvA vAyusutasya ha#} <ls>Rām. 6. 18. 1</ls>.
.²9 The understanding; <ab>cf.</ab> {#AtmasaMpanna, Atmavat#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²10 Thinking faculty, the faculty of thought and reason.
.²11 Spirit, vitality, courage; {#tyaktvA''tmAnamaTAbravIt#} <ls>Mb. 12. 180. 6</ls>.
.²12 Form, image; {#AtmAnamADAya#} <ls>Ku. 3. 24</ls> assuming his own form; <ls n="Ku.">2. 61</ls>;
 {#saMropite'pyAtmani#} <ls>Ś. 6. 24</ls> myself being implanted in her.
.²13 A son; {#‘AtmA vE putranAmAsi’ iti SruteH . tasyAtmA SitikaRWasya#} <ls>Śi. 2. 61</ls>.
.²14 Care, efforts, pain.
.²15 The sun.
.²16 Fire.
.²17 Wind, air.
.²18 Mental quality; {#bAhuSrutyaM tapastyAgaH SradDA yajYakriyA kzamA .#}
 {#BAvaSudDirdayA satyaM saMyamaScAtmasaMpadaH ..#} <ls>Mb. 12. 167. 5</ls>. {#Atman#}
 is used as the last member of <ab>comp.</ab> in the sense of ‘made or consisting
 of’; see {#Atmaka#}. The form {#tman#} is also found to be used; {#kftArTaM#}
 {#manyate tmAnaM#} <ls>Mb.</ls> [<ab>cf.</ab> <lang>Gr.</lang> {%atmos, aitmen%}]

one who pretends to belong to a higher class than
 his own, an impostor, a pretender; {#yo'nyaTA santamAtmAnamanyaTA satsu#}
 {#BAzate . sa pApakfttamo loke stena AtmApahArakaH ..#} <ls>Ms. 4. 255</ls>.

.²1 loving oneself, possessed of self-conceit, proud; {#AtmakAmA sadA caRqI#}
 <ls>Rām. 2. 70. 10</ls>.
.²2 loving Brahman or the Supreme Spirit only; {#Bagavan vayamAtmakAmAH#}
 <ls>Maitr. Up. 7. 10</ls>.

.²1 self-executed, done by oneself; {#pOrA hyAtmakftAdduHKAdvipramocyA#}
 {#nfpAtmajEH#} <ls>Rām. 2. 46. 23</ls>.
.²2 done against oneʼs own self; <ls>Vāj. 8. 13</ls>.

.²1 a suicide, a self-destroyer; <ls>K. 174</ls>; {#vyApAdayed vfTAtmAnaM svayaM#}
 {#yo'gnyudakAdiBiH . avEDenEva mArgeRa AtmaGAtI sa ucyate ..#}
.²2 a heretic.

.²1 a son; {#yaH sa vAsavanirjetA rAvaRasyAtmasaMBavaH#} <ls>Rām. 6. 86. 33</ls>;
 {#hatAnnihanmeha nararzaBeRa vayaM sureSAtmasamudBavena#} <ls>Mb. 7. 118. 2</ls>;
 {#tamAtmajanmAnamajaM cakAra#} <ls>R. 5. 36</ls>; {#tasyAmAtmAnurUpAyAmAtmajanmasamutsukaH#}
 <ls>R. 1. 33</ls>; <ls>Māl. 1</ls>; <ls>Ku. 6. 28</ls>.
.²2 Cupid; {#mamAyamAtmapraBavo BUyastvamupayAsyati#} <ls>Rām. 4. 1. 34</ls>.
.²3 a descendant; {#mfgayAM vicarankaScidvijane janakAtmajaH#} <ls>Mb. 12. 309. 1</ls>.

.²1 seeing oneself.
.²2 spiritual knowledge, true wisdom; {#sarvaBUtAtmadarSanam#} <ls>Y. 3. 157</ls>;
 <ab>cf.</ab> <ls>Ms. 12. 91</ls>; see {#AtmayAjin#}.

.²1 oneʼs own kinsman; {#AtmamAtuH svasuH putrA AtmapituH svasuH sutAH .#}
 {#AtmamAtulaputrASca vijYeyA hyAtmabAnDavAH#} <ls>Śabdak.</ls> {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%}

 motherʼs sisterʼs son, fatherʼs sisterʼs son, and motherʼs brotherʼs son.
.²2 the soul, the self.

self-respecting, respectable.
.²2 arrogant, proud; {#vivekaSUnyaH praBurAtmamAnI, mahAnanarTaH suhfdAM#}
 {#batAyam#} <ls>Bk. 12. 83</ls>.

.²1 sacrificing for oneself or himself. {%m.%} a learned
 man who studies his own nature and that of the soul (of others) to secure
 eternal felicity, one who looks upon all beings as self; {#sarvaBUtezu#}
 {#cAtmAnaM sarvaBUtAni cAtmani . samaM paSyannAtmayAjI svArAjyamaDigacCati ..#}
 <ls>Ms. 12. 91</ls>.

depending on oneʼs own will; {#yadyatparavaSaM karma#}
 {#tattadyatnena varjayet . yadyadAtmavaSaM tu syAttattatseveta yatnataH .#}
 <ls>Ms. 4. 159</ls>, {#sarvamAtmavaSaM suKam#} <ls n="Ms. 4.">160</ls>.
.

.²1 oneʼs own power or ability, inherent power or effort; {#dEvaM nihatya#}
 {#kuru pOruzamAtmaSaktyA#} <ls>Pt. 1. 361</ls> to the best of oneʼs power.
.²2 illusion.
